                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "UBERMOSH:WRAITH has a fast-paced arcade concept, but the gameplay feels repetitive and can become frustrating after only a short time. The combat is intense, but the high difficulty makes it difficult to enjoy the experience, especially when mistakes are punished so quickly. While the minimalist visuals and action-focused design may appeal to fans of arcade shooters, there isn't enough variety to keep things interesting for long. The gameplay loop starts to feel more like repeating the same challenge than making meaningful progress, and the overall experience can become exhausting rather than entertaining. It's not necessarily a bad game for players who enjoy punishing difficulty, but it didn't offer enough depth or variety to keep me engaged.",
